Source: thunderbolt-net
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Shun Li <riverscn@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-sequence-dkms, python3, git
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: thunderbolt-net-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dkms (>= 3.0.10)
Description: experimental Thunderbolt networking RX normalization (DKMS)
 Out-of-tree thunderbolt_net replacement with validation and
 segmentation metadata for oversized TCP packets received from a peer.
 It preserves aggregates for local delivery and allows Linux to segment
 supported packets when forwarding requires it.
 .
 This package contains source, built by DKMS for the target kernel.
 A modprobe file in /usr/lib/modprobe.d enables the workaround and RX page
 recycling on the next module load; override it from /etc/modprobe.d.
 Installation does not request unloading or reloading an active network module.
